# Architecture

## Technology stack

- Python 3.12+, FastAPI, Pydantic, pytest, Ruff, and uv.

## Component architecture

- `main.py` defines HTTP boundaries and dependency injection.
- `providers/` defines the provider protocol, an offline mock, and only the selected external adapters.
- `prompts/` stores prompt text outside Python code.
{% if rag %}- The in-memory retrieval seam provides deterministic local RAG behavior and can later be replaced behind the same boundary.
{% endif %}
## Data flow

Validated API input is combined with a versioned prompt template and passed to the configured provider. The default provider is deterministic and local. External clients are constructed only when selected and invoked.

## Security considerations

Never accept provider keys in request bodies, log prompts only under an explicit data policy, validate uploaded/document inputs, and grant Bedrock permissions only for required models and actions.

## Deployment approach

Run with uvicorn locally. External AI providers, vector stores, workers, and cloud deployment remain opt-in.

